  "abstract": {
    "value": "An asymmetric organocatalytic remote 1,10-addition of alkynyl indole imine methides generated in situ from α-(6- indolyl) propargylic alcohols with thiazolones has been developed for the first time, affording axially chiral tetrasubstituted allenes featuring vicinal sulfur-containing quaternary carbon stereocenters in high yields with excellent stereoselectivities. The representative scale-up reaction and transformations of the 1,10-adduct were examined. The reaction mechanism was expounded by control experiments and DFT calculations. ![](../extracted/org.-lett.-2022-24-4914/images/b7d3e40f72ccec2f2d7aac6d80df8eae8e172e78d3fd2a609021a8177f38f7e2.jpg) <details> <summary>chemical</summary> Chemical reaction scheme showing conversion of racemic α-(6-indolyl) propargylic alcohols to a heterocyclic compound with 32 examples, yielding 86-96% ee and 6:1-15:1 dr </details> A symmetric organocatalytic Michael additions have been well-developed for stereocontrolled construction of chiral carbon−carbon and carbon−heteroatom bonds (Scheme 1A).1",
    "source": "markdown_inline_abstract",
